---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import keelBrowser from '../../assets/keel/keel-browser.png';
import keelCli from '../../assets/keel/keel-cli-welcome.png';

const facts = [
  ['Role', 'Idea, design and build, solo'],
  ['Stack', 'TypeScript · pnpm monorepo · libSQL · Mintlify'],
  ['License', 'MIT, open source from the first commit'],
  ['Status', 'v0.4.0 on npm · Goals in progress'],
];

const links = [
  ['Read the docs', 'https://nouisi-keel.mintlify.site'],
  ['Keel on GitHub', 'https://github.com/upadhyayprakash/keel'],
  ['@nouisi/keel on npm', 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/@nouisi/keel'],
];

const failures = [
  ['Promises', 'Missed: "I\'ll send it Friday" slipped.'],
  ['Priorities', 'The wrong thing got the day.'],
  ['Context', 'Coming back to a project cost 30 minutes of "where was I?"'],
  ['Decisions', 'Rushed, with no record of why.'],
];

const built = [
  ['One core, two terminals', 'A shared core does all the work, so a feature written once appears in the CLI, the shell and the browser at the same time.'],
  ['Commands return blocks, not text', 'A command never prints. It returns blocks with meaning attached, and each terminal renders them in its own way.'],
  ['Ready for a hosted database', 'v1 only needed a local file, but the storage rules meant multi-device sync needed no data model changes.'],
];
---

<Base title="Keel, Prakash Upadhyay" description="Keel, an open-source terminal app for promises, priorities and project context, and the goal mode being built into it." current="work" progress>
  <section class="head" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <div class="head__in">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/work">Work</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Keel</span></p>
      <h1 id="page-title">Keel</h1>
      <p class="head__tag">Promises. Priorities. Context.</p>
      <p class="head__text">A terminal app that tracks what you owe, what you're waiting on, your focus for today and where you left each project. Your data stays in a local file.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <main>
    <div class="top">
      <Image class="shot" src={keelBrowser} alt="keel serve in the browser, showing today: focus, waiting-on follow-ups and what's coming up." widths={[640, 1040]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 760px" />
      <aside aria-label="Project facts">
        {facts.map(([k, v]) => <div><p class="label">{k}</p><p class="fact">{v}</p></div>)}
        <div class="links">{links.map(([t, href]) => <a href={href}>{t}</a>)}</div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <section aria-labelledby="problem-title">
      <div class="rule"><h2 id="problem-title">The problem</h2><div aria-hidden="true"></div></div>
      <p class="lead">Keel started as a personal annoyance: working on many things at once kept failing in the same four ways.</p>
      <ul class="grid">
        {failures.map(([t, d]) => <li><h3>{t}</h3><p>{d}</p></li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="design" aria-labelledby="design-title">
      <div class="rule"><h2 id="design-title">The design pivot</h2><div aria-hidden="true"></div></div>
      <div class="split">
        <Image class="shot" src={keelCli} alt="The Keel shell in a terminal: the logo, today with focus and follow-ups, and the prompt showing the current project." widths={[480, 800]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 520px" />
        <div class="split__text">
          <p class="lead">The first plan had a full web UI and a phone layout. Claude drew those screens as a canvas of boards in an artifact, next to the terminal ones.</p>
          <p>Seeing them side by side made the call easy. I parked the graphical web app, dropped the phone and kept one terminal experience in two places: one command language, rendered twice, instead of two products.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="built-title">
      <div class="rule"><h2 id="built-title">How it is built</h2><div aria-hidden="true"></div></div>
      <ul class="grid">
        {built.map(([t, d]) => <li><h3>{t}</h3><p>{d}</p></li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="goals-title">
      <div class="rule"><h2 id="goals-title">Goals in Keel</h2><div aria-hidden="true"></div></div>
      <p class="lead">A goal mode for small personal goals with a finish line, days to a few weeks away, with a phone app served by <code>keel serve</code>.</p>
      <p>People rarely fail at such goals for lack of a list. They fail because the goal is vague, one missed day turns into quitting, or the last 10% drifts. So a finish line and an if-then plan are required before a goal can be saved.</p>
      <p class="status"><span>In progress</span>Merged to <code>main</code> and documented. Not in a release yet: it's planned for 0.5.0.</p>
      <div class="links links--row">
        <a href="https://nouisi-keel.mintlify.site/guides/goals">Goals guide</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/upadhyayprakash/keel/blob/25a568ec0a1c26c24bac20e3710038f5642903b8/docs/adr/0004-goals.md">ADR 0004</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .head {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .head__in {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 72px clamp(16px, 4vw, 40px) 80px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }

  .crumbs {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    font-family: var(--font-label);
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-weight: var(--weight-label);
  }

  .crumbs a {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(48px, 7vw, 96px);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 0.98;
  }

  .head__tag {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 30px);
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .head__text {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 640px;
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  main {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 72px clamp(16px, 4vw, 40px) 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 120px;
  }

  section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    scroll-margin-top: 96px;
  }

  section p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  section .lead {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--display);
  }

  .top {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 32px 64px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .top :global(.shot) {
    flex: 1 1 560px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .shot {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card-lg);
  }

  aside {
    flex: 0 1 300px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }

  aside > div:not(.links) {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  .label {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-label);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-weight: var(--weight-label);
  }

  .fact {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .links {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .links--row {
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-6);
    border-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .links a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: var(--touch-target);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .rule {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .rule div {
    flex: 1;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-label);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: var(--weight-label);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .grid {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(240px, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .grid li {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .grid p {
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .split {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 32px 64px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .split :global(.shot) {
    flex: 0 1 420px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .split__text {
    flex: 1 1 340px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .status {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
  }

  .status span {
    border: 1px solid var(--outline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    padding: 6px 14px;
    font-family: var(--font-label);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: var(--weight-label);
  }
</style>
